# Backend Route Patterns

## Route Setup

- Use Express router objects for route organization
- Import router objects directly (never use dynamic `require()` paths)
- Apply middleware at the router level when appropriate

## Error Handling

Routes call controller functions. Controllers handle errors using `return next(new ErrorClass())` pattern. Routes themselves don't handle errors directly - they delegate to controllers.

## Testing Routes

- Use `createExpressTestApp` utility for route testing
- Set environment variables at top level before imports
- Always cleanup in `afterEach`

## Summary

- Use router objects for organization
- Import routers directly
- Controllers handle error passing to middleware
